// A gate whose meaning depends on the EVENT SCHEMA, not on anything written here.
//
//     permit a Trade if this principal was approved within the hour
//
// Read the text and that is all it says. Replayed under the three shipped event-schema presets it
// means three different things, because a universal pin partitions the history a temporal
// predicate can see and no policy can observe or bypass one:
//
//   pinned.dwschema (DEFAULT)  the approval must be the same PRINCIPAL's
//   session-pinned.dwschema    it must also be in the same SESSION -- a concurrent session of the
//                              same user no longer counts
//   unpinned.dwschema          any approval anywhere in the trace counts
//
// `dogwood_replay.py` runs the middle two against the engine. The corpus cannot: across its 521
// cases a top-level `pin sessionId = context.sessionId` appears zero times, though it is a shipped
// preset one deployment flag away from the default.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Anchor::Action::"Trade",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Anchor::Action::"Approve"::request{ input.approver: "alice" }
};
